  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`. I added `test/satisfies.test.js` with 11 tests, and `npm test` passes (12 of 12, counting the existing placeholder test).\n\nThe tests cover each part of the spec: invalid input, `v` prefixes and build metadata, comparators, prerelease ordering, wildcards, partial versions, tilde, caret, hyphen ranges, `||`, and the prerelease rule. I didn't have an independent reference implementation to check against, so the tests only check my reading of the spec.\n\nWhere the spec was silent, I chose these behaviours:\n- **Empty `||` branches:** an empty branch such as `1.0.0 ||` matches any version, as an empty range does.\n- **Spaces after `~` and `^`:** `~ 1.2.3` is invalid and returns `false`. The spec only allows a space after the comparator operators.\n- **Wildcards:** a wildcard makes every later position a wildcard too, so `1.x.3` is read as `1.x`.\n- **Prerelease on a partial:** a prerelease on a partial version, such as `1.2.x-beta`, is invalid.\n- **Number size:** numbers are compared as `BigInt`, so very large version numbers don't lose precision.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
